WEBVTT

00:01:57.538 --> 00:02:00.246
Instead of installing solar panels
around a planet,

00:02:00.288 --> 00:02:04.413
a Type II civilization would install them
directly orbiting its star,

00:02:04.454 --> 00:02:07.496
forming a theoretical structure
called a Dyson sphere.

00:02:07.538 --> 00:02:09.704
And the third step?

00:02:09.913 --> 00:02:14.538
A Type III civilization would harness
all the energy of its home galaxy.

00:02:14.579 --> 00:02:17.496
But we can also think of progress
in the opposite way.

00:02:17.538 --> 00:02:19.913
How small can we go?

00:02:21.163 --> 00:02:23.288
To that end, British 
cosmologist John Barrow

00:02:23.329 --> 00:02:27.538
classified civilizations by the size
of the objects they control.

00:02:28.079 --> 00:02:30.788
That ranges from mechanical structures
at our own scale,